hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22857","Bahz and Abu an-Nadr said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, who said: al-Walid came to me, me and a companion of mine. He said: So he said to us: Come, for you two are younger than me and more retentive of hadith than me. He said: So he went with us to Bishr ibn Asim. He said: So Abu al-Aliyah said to him: Narrate your hadith to these two. He said: Uqbah ibn Malik narrated to us, Abu an-Nadr said al-Laythi, Bahz said and he was of his clan, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent a detachment. He said: So it raided a people. He said: So a man strayed from the people. He said: So a man of the detachment followed him brandishing his sword. He said: So the stray one of the people said: Indeed I am a Muslim. He said: So he did not consider what he said, and struck him and killed him. He said: So the report reached the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: So he said about it a severe saying. So it reached the killer. He said: So while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was delivering a sermon, the killer said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, what he said, he said only seeking refuge from killing. He said: So he turned away from him and from those near him of the people, and continued his sermon. Then he said again: O Messenger of Allah, what he said, he said only seeking refuge from killing. So he turned away from him and from those near him of the people, and continued his sermon. Then he could not be patient, so he said a third time: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he said it only seeking refuge from killing. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, turned to him with displeasure recognized in his face. He said to him: Indeed Allah, mighty and majestic, refused for one who killed a believer, three times."
